FL,305,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30408
SC,0008
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F304A1785975492
OL,3,CPeter Duncan calls for approval of
OL,4,C'life-changing' prostate cancer
OL,5,Ctreatment
OL,7,FAccording to Prostate Cancer UK, the
OL,8,Fcondition is the most common cancer in
OL,9,Fmen and one in eight men will receive
OL,10,Fa diagnosis in their lifetime, with
OL,11,Fthe risk increasing if you are over
OL,12,F50, black, or have a family history of
OL,13,Fthe disease.
OL,15,FProstate cancer develops slowly so
OL,16,Fthere may be no signs for years,
OL,17,Fthough symptoms may include an
OL,18,Fincreased need to urinate, straining
OL,19,Fwhile urinating and a feeling that the
OL,20,Fbladder has not fully emptied,
OL,21,Faccording to the NHS.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G8/8
